/*  The parser's hold on its tokens: where it stands, what comes next, and how it refuses.

    ★ Each helper here is a port of the one in `src/Interpreter/Parser.cs` with the same name, in
    the same order of tests, because the parity test compares TREES and a lookahead that asks its
    questions in a different order builds a different tree on exactly the inputs nobody thought of.

    ★ A token's kind is the C# enum's name, spelled exactly, so the two parsers read one vocabulary.

    Two ways to stop, both failures, both carrying line, column and reason tab-separated:
    - `refused`, for a source the C# parser also refuses (`error` in the output);
    - `not-yet`, for a construct this parser has not been taught (`unsupported`) — the parity test
      lists those files rather than failing them, so the parser can be written a piece at a time.
*/

Pull a book on collections.
    Define object parser with (
        the series of token tokens,
        the number at,
        the number type-depth,
        the number collections-depth,
        the number loop-depth,
        the number nest-depth,
        the number function-depth,
        the fact in-object-def,
        the fact in-free-function).

    // ── Where the parser stands ───────────────────────────────────────────

    /// The token at `spot`, or the last one (Eof) past the end.
    Bind token to token-at unto parser, given (the number spot):
        If spot is greater than the number of one's tokens, return the last of one's tokens.
        Return item spot of one's tokens.
    Done.

    Bind token to peek unto parser:
        Return cast one's token-at on (one's at).
    Done.

    Bind text to peek-kind unto parser:
        Define current as cast one's token-at on (one's at).
        Return current's kind.
    Done.

    Bind token to advance unto parser:
        Define current as cast one's token-at on (one's at).
        Increment one's at by 1.
        Return current.
    Done.

    /// The token just consumed.
    Bind token to previous unto parser:
        Return cast one's token-at on (one's at - 1).
    Done.

    Bind fact to is-noise, given (the token candidate):
        Return candidate's kind is "Article".
    Done.

    /// Where the first token past any noise sits, looking from `spot`.
    Bind number to past-noise unto parser, given (the number spot):
        Define found as spot.
        While cast is-noise on (cast one's token-at on (found)), repeat:
            Increment found by 1.
        Done.
        Return found.
    Done.

    /// PeekAfterCurrent — the first non-noise token after the current one.
    Bind text to kind-after unto parser:
        Define found as cast one's token-at on (cast one's past-noise on (one's at + 1)).
        Return found's kind.
    Done.

    /// PeekTwoAfterCurrent.
    Bind text to kind-two-after unto parser:
        Define second-spot as cast one's past-noise on (cast one's past-noise on (one's at + 1) + 1).
        Define found as cast one's token-at on (second-spot).
        Return found's kind.
    Done.

    /// PeekSkippingNoise — the current token's kind, looking past noise.
    Bind text to kind-past-noise unto parser:
        Define found as cast one's token-at on (cast one's past-noise on (one's at)).
        Return found's kind.
    Done.

    /// PeekPastNoiseIs — past one comma and any noise.
    Bind fact to past-comma-is unto parser, given (the text kind):
        Define spot as one's at.
        Define here as cast one's token-at on (spot).
        If here's kind is "Comma", increment spot by 1.
        Define found as cast one's token-at on (cast one's past-noise on (spot)).
        Return found's kind is kind.
    Done.

    Bind fact to spelled, given (the token candidate, the text word):
        Return (candidate's lexeme in lowercase) is word.
    Done.

    /// IsWord — the current token is spelled `word`, whatever kind it is.
    Bind fact to is-word unto parser, given (the text word):
        Return cast spelled on (cast one's peek, word).
    Done.

    /// NextWordIs / PeekAfterCurrentIsWord — the first non-noise token after the current one.
    Bind fact to next-word-is unto parser, given (the text word):
        Return cast spelled on (cast one's token-at on (cast one's past-noise on (one's at + 1)), word).
    Done.

    /// IsWordAfterCurrent — skips articles only.
    Bind fact to word-after-is unto parser, given (the text word):
        Return cast one's next-word-is on (word).
    Done.

    // ── Refusing ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    Bind text to refusal-at, given (the text shape, the token spot-tok, the text reason):
        Return "{shape}\t{spot-tok's row}\t{spot-tok's column}\t{reason}".
    Done.

    /// A construct this parser has not been taught yet.
    Bind text to not-yet unto parser, given (the text what):
        Return cast refusal-at on ("unsupported", cast one's peek, what).
    Done.

    /// A source the C# parser refuses too.
    Bind text to refused unto parser, given (the token spot-tok, the text reason):
        Return cast refusal-at on ("error", spot-tok, reason).
    Done.

    Bind token or failure to consume unto parser, given (the text kind):
        Define current as cast one's peek.
        If current's kind is not kind:
            Return a failure (cast one's refused on (current,
                "expected {kind}, got {current's kind} \"{current's lexeme}\"")).
        Done.
        Return cast one's advance.
    Done.

    // ── Noise ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// Articles are noise — except a `the` that opens `the <name> of <thing>`.
    Bind void to skip-noise unto parser:
        While cast is-noise on (cast one's peek), repeat:
            If cast one's is-word on ("the") and cast one's is-named-access-pattern, stop.
            Cast one's advance.
        Done.
    Done.

    /// SkipNoiseBeforeType — in a type position no `the` opens a field access.
    Bind void to skip-noise-before-type unto parser:
        Increment one's type-depth by 1.
        Cast one's skip-noise.
        Decrement one's type-depth by 1.
    Done.

    // ── What a word is here ───────────────────────────────────────────────

    Bind fact to is-ordinal-lexeme, given (the text lexeme):
        Define lowered as lexeme in lowercase.
        For each ordinal in a series with ("first", "second", "third", "fourth", "fifth", "sixth",
                "seventh", "eighth", "ninth", "tenth", "last"), repeat:
            If lowered is ordinal, return true.
        Done.
        Return false.
    Done.

    /// Tokens that can never be the FIRST token of a value — see CannotBeginAValue.
    Bind fact to cannot-begin-a-value, given (the text kind):
        For each shut in a series with (
                "Plus", "Star", "Slash", "Percent", "Equal", "Lt", "Gt", "Lte", "Gte", "NotEqual",
                "For", "From", "To", "In", "Into", "Unto", "Through", "On", "As", "By", "Than",
                "Is", "And", "Or", "Xor", "But", "Has", "Contains", "Joined", "Converted", "Split",
                "Like", "Becomes", "Sorted", "Trimmed", "Shifted", "Reverse", "Uppercase",
                "Lowercase", "DirectoryKw"), repeat:
            If kind is shut, return true.
        Done.
        Return false.
    Done.

    /// IsFieldNameToken.
    Bind fact to is-field-name, given (the token candidate, the fact for-access):
        Define kind as candidate's kind.
        For each shut in a series with (
                "Of", "Dot", "Colon", "LParen", "RParen", "Comma", "Number", "String", "Plus",
                "Minus", "Star", "Slash", "Percent", "Equal", "Lt", "Gt", "Lte", "Gte", "NotEqual",
                "Eof"), repeat:
            If kind is shut, return false.
        Done.
        Define is-the as kind is "Article" and cast spelled on (candidate, "the").
        If is-the, return false.
        If for-access:
            Define other-article as kind is "Article" and is-the is false.
            If kind is not "Identifier" and kind is not "Category" and other-article is false:
                Return false.
            Done.
            If kind is "Identifier" and cast is-ordinal-lexeme on (candidate's lexeme), return false.
        Done.
        Return true.
    Done.

    /// IsNamedAccessPattern — `the <name> of <something that can begin a value>`.
    Bind fact to is-named-access-pattern unto parser:
        If one's type-depth is greater than 0, return false.
        Define spot as one's at + 1.
        If cast is-field-name on (cast one's token-at on (spot), true) is false, return false.
        Define following as cast one's token-at on (cast one's past-noise on (spot + 1)).
        If following's kind is not "Of", return false.
        Define target as cast one's token-at on (cast one's past-noise on (cast one's past-noise on (spot + 1) + 1)).
        Return cast cannot-begin-a-value on (target's kind) is false.
    Done.

    /// BindsToWhatFollows — a `-` written against the value after it.
    Bind fact to binds-to-what-follows unto parser, given (the number spot):
        Define sign as cast one's token-at on (spot).
        Define value as cast one's token-at on (spot + 1).
        Return value's row is sign's row and value's column is sign's column + the length of sign's lexeme.
    Done.

    /// IsNamedFieldStart — `the <name> <value>`.
    Bind fact to is-named-field-start unto parser:
        Define here as cast one's peek.
        If here's kind is not "Article" or cast spelled on (here, "the") is false, return false.
        If cast is-field-name on (cast one's token-at on (one's at + 1), false) is false, return false.
        Define spot as cast one's past-noise on (one's at + 2).
        Define following as cast one's token-at on (spot).
        If following's kind is "Of", return false.
        If cast cannot-begin-a-value on (following's kind), return false.
        If following's kind is "Minus", return cast one's binds-to-what-follows on (spot).
        Return true.
    Done.

    /// EffectiveType — what a word acts as HERE. Book words lex as identifiers so they stay usable
    /// as names, and a mandatory next word is what tells the shape apart.
    Bind text to effective-kind unto parser, given (the token candidate):
        If candidate's kind is not "Identifier", return candidate's kind.
        Define lowered as candidate's lexeme in lowercase.
        Define following as cast one's kind-after.
        If lowered is "current" and following is "DirectoryKw", return "CurrentKw".
        If lowered is "matrix" and following is "With", return "Matrix".
        If lowered is "chase" and one's collections-depth is greater than 0, return "Chase".
        If lowered is "randomly" and cast one's next-word-is on ("shuffled"), return "Randomly".
        If lowered is "random":
            If following is "NumberKw" or following is "Item" or cast one's next-word-is on ("guess"):
                Return "Random".
            Done.
        Done.
        If lowered is "channel" and following is "Of", return "Channel".
        If lowered is "characters" and following is "From", return "Characters".
        If lowered is "delivery" and following is "From", return "Delivery".
        If lowered is "entry" and following is "For", return "Entry".
        If lowered is "key" and following is "For", return "Key".
        If lowered is "interrupt" and following is "Is", return "InterruptKw".
        If lowered is "environment" and cast one's next-word-is on ("variable"), return "EnvironmentKw".
        If lowered is "read":
            If cast one's next-word-is on ("line") or cast one's next-word-is on ("all"), return "Read".
        Done.
        If lowered is "contents" and following is "Of":
            Define beyond as cast one's token-at on (cast one's past-noise on (cast one's past-noise on (one's at + 1) + 1)).
            If beyond's kind is "DirectoryKw", return "ContentsKw".
        Done.
        Return candidate's kind.
    Done.
Done.
